          "description": "Append a durable note to one scheduled request. Notes record why a\nschedule exists and what changed and when. Wake metadata includes the message,\nschedule identity, timing and an optional title; it does not include notes.\nWhen execution depends on a note, ensure the schedule's message explicitly\ntells the Keeper to call masc_schedule_notes_list with its schedule ID before\nacting. Use masc_schedule_update while the schedule is editable to add that\ninstruction. Adding a note alone neither changes the message nor signals that\nnotes need reading. Notes are keyed by the stable schedule_id, so replacing a\ndefinition does not orphan them. Notes are append-only, with no edit or removal,\nand survive terminal schedule states. You are recorded as the author.",
